Package: macodgent
Title: Toolkit for Routine Medical Data Science Analysis
Version: 1.1.0
Date: 2026-11-08
Authors@R: c(person(given = "Xie YJ", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "xiemacodgent@163.com"), person(given = "MA Codgent",
    role = c("cph")))
Maintainer: Xie YJ <xiemacodgent@163.com>
Description: A collection of reusable analysis functions implementing the Routine Analysis Techniques for
    medical-data-science workflows. It covers data preprocessing, quantitative
    and qualitative descriptive statistics, conventional and advanced regression,
    survival analysis, competing-risk models, and models for transitions
    between multiple states.
    All exported functions use the 'mc_' prefix. Descriptive statistics and
    hypothesis tests return tidy data frames; model-fitting functions return a
    list containing the fitted model, a coefficient table and, where applicable,
    a ggplot2 plot. Hypothesis tests report effect sizes with confidence
    intervals and multiplicity-adjusted p values; logistic and survival models
    include discrimination, calibration, collinearity, influence and
    proportional-hazards checks. A shared check layer gives linear, logistic
    and Cox models the same pass/review verdict shape. Twelve model families
    are reachable through one uniform dispatcher. A one-call automated
    analysis returns a complete result bundle, records each automatic
    decision, and can write a standalone HTML report and CSV tables.
